  "headline": "Bond market is pricing a hot economy, and gold is paying for it",
  "body": [
    "The configuration is reflation running into a higher-rate response. The 10-year yield sits at a 52-week high of 5.11%, up 15 basis points today and 41 over the month, while the 30-year has added only 17 over the same month, flattening the 30y–10y spread by 24 basis points to 29. That is a bear flattener: the market is repricing the policy path higher on strong growth and inflation, not fretting about long-run fiscal risk. The dollar confirms it, up 2.2% on the month to the top of its range.",
    "Growth is the anchor. Copper is up 4.8% this week and 20% year-to-date, sitting at 94% of its range, and the copper/gold ratio has climbed 11% over the month. Brent near $98 is up 60% year-to-date, the inflation impulse in the mix, even after a 7% pullback this week. Gold's 8% monthly fall is the tell: it is selling off because real yields and the dollar are rising, not because anyone is hiding. Bitcoin outrunning gold by 18% over the month says liquidity and risk appetite remain intact.",
    "The tension is today's session: yields jumped and every dollar-priced asset fell together, gold 1.7%, copper 1.9%, bitcoin 2.5%. Part of that is simply the dollar's 0.6% gain. On the month, though, the industrial and risk signals outweigh a one-day flinch; this is a strong-economy repricing, not a growth scare."
